(448255, 41640, 12448, '<td valign="top">Talk about over exposured!  I''m guessing it''s a flashlight behind the negative to help with the lighting, the center shot of yellow is sadly, very distracting.  The sides and negative itself is well done, but the coloring just seems a bit off to me.  Starting with a 6, will be back to think about it again.</td>', 'Talk about over exposured!  I''m guessing it''s a flashlight behind the negative to help with the lighting, the center shot of yellow is sadly, very distracting.  The sides and negative itself is well done, but the coloring just seems a bit off to me.  Starting with a 6, will be back to think about it again.', '2003-10-13 01:56:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(448256, 42008, 12448, '<td valign="top">Ewwwwwwwwwww!  LOLOL!  What a great idea!  I also thought about doing the same thing, only with my barfy dog, ick!  Glad I didn''t!  The colors are wonderful the orange and the fresh innards.  The light is just a bit off, to bright at the bottom, more evened would have scored you a 9 or 10 right off the bat, starting with an 8, will be back to look again.</td>', 'Ewwwwwwwwwww!  LOLOL!  What a great idea!  I also thought about doing the same thing, only with my barfy dog, ick!  Glad I didn''t!  The colors are wonderful the orange and the fresh innards.  The light is just a bit off, to bright at the bottom, more evened would have scored you a 9 or 10 right off the bat, starting with an 8, will be back to look again.', '2003-10-13 01:58:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(448258, 41901, 9441, '<td valign="top">very creative showing the step by step process.</td>', 'very creative showing the step by step process.', '2003-10-13 01:58:48.000000', NULL, 1),
